WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:07.176
Hi! Today we count to a hundred – and beyond!

2
00:00:07.576 --> 00:00:11.112
And you ask: How much is that?

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.376
These are the tens:

4
00:00:15.776 --> 00:00:17.848
twenty

5
00:00:18.248 --> 00:00:22.264
thirty. With ß!

6
00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:24.736
forty

7
00:00:25.136 --> 00:00:27.232
fifty

8
00:00:27.632 --> 00:00:29.704
sixty

9
00:00:30.104 --> 00:00:32.176
a hundred

10
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:39.971
Now a trick: in German we say the ones first, then the tens.

11
00:00:40.371 --> 00:00:44.891
twenty-one. One and twenty.

12
00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:47.363
Listen:

13
00:00:47.763 --> 00:00:50.099
twenty-one

14
00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:52.931
thirty-four

15
00:00:53.331 --> 00:00:55.979
fifty-seven

16
00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:00.675
At the flea market you ask:

17
00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:03.843
How much is the table?

18
00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:07.227
It costs thirty euros.

19
00:01:07.627 --> 00:01:12.291
And this is how we say prices: two euros fifty.

20
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.952
A hundred euros for a chair? Then you say:

21
00:01:19.352 --> 00:01:21.880
That's too expensive!

22
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.944
Two euros for a lamp? Great:

23
00:01:27.344 --> 00:01:29.680
That's cheap!

24
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.928
Or more friendly: Das ist günstig (good value).

25
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:39.889
Listen: Lena is at the flea market.

26
00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:43.153
How much is the lamp?

27
00:01:43.553 --> 00:01:45.793
Twelve euros.

28
00:01:46.193 --> 00:01:48.385
And the chair?

29
00:01:48.785 --> 00:01:51.505
Twenty-five euros.

30
00:01:51.905 --> 00:01:54.433
That's too expensive!

31
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:57.985
Okay, twenty euros.

32
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:07.748
Now you! Count out loud from twenty to a hundred: twenty, thirty, forty…

33
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:21.569
Great! Now you can:

34
00:02:21.969 --> 00:02:26.153
You count to a hundred and ask about prices.

35
00:02:26.553 --> 00:02:28.673
See you soon!
